.TE
.PP
Each COMMAND node includes: \f[CR]\(dqtype\(dq\f[R] (enum name string),
\f[CR]\(dqflags\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqline\(dq\f[R], optional
\f[CR]\(dqredirects\(dq\f[R], and the type\-specific sub\-object.
.PP
Words are serialized as
\f[CR]{\(dqword\(dq:\(dqtext\(dq,\(dqflags\(dq:N}\f[R] arrays.
Redirects include \f[CR]instruction\f[R], \f[CR]redirector\f[R],
\f[CR]flags\f[R], \f[CR]rflags\f[R], \f[CR]filename\f[R] or
\f[CR]dest\f[R], and optional \f[CR]here_doc_eof\f[R].
.PP
Uses a growable string buffer (\f[CR]serbuf_t\f[R]) internally for
efficient JSON construction.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]cmd\f[R] \(em Pointer to a bash \f[CR]COMMAND\f[R] structure.
May be NULL, in which case the string \f[CR]\(dqnull\(dq\f[R] is
returned.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a \f[CR]malloc()\f[R]\(cqd JSON string that the caller must
\f[CR]free()\f[R].
.PP
Returns the string \f[CR]\(dqnull\(dq\f[R] (via \f[CR]strdup\f[R]) if
\f[B]cmd\f[R] is NULL.
.PP
Returns NULL if memory allocation fails during buffer initialization.
